WEBVTT

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.820
What?!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.040
Destroy!

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.210
All right!

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:41.810
Iceman!

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.350
Destroy!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.980
Basquash!

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.590
Iceman!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.630
Nice pass-!

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.790
Huh? Tampon shop?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.670
Championship.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.250
And guess who it's from?

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.000
The good old OCB Commission themselves!

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.130
Didn't they ban us?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.810
The way you guys have been cleaning up lately,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.180
it looks like they can no longer afford <i>not</i> to invite you.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.640
Everyone's telling 'em to invite Team Basquash and generating a huge fuss on the Net.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.760
So, where are they gonna hold it?

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.230
Turbine City.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.400
Turbine... City.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.710
BEFORE
IN
THE
NIGHT

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.200
The wind...

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.030
...decides victory and defeat.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.860
It's in the air...

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.370
This place is bustling with activity, isn't it?

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.360
Yes!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.160
The excitement of the people waiting for the festival to begin

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.140
has spread throughout the whole town.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.810
Whoops!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.710
That's some wind!

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.610
The main industry in this town is the generation of wind power.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.900
As the town itself collects the many scattered winds into one,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.940
it results in an incredible force being unleashed.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.770
The hubbub of city life on the wind...

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.390
The scent of the water...

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.670
But you know, for somewhere called Turpentine City, it don't smell half bad.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.240
It's not Turpentine City.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.920
It's Turbine City; the city of wind.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.840
But is it really all right for us to have a match in a town that's so densely built?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.560
It'll be fine.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.070
This says the buildings are really tough, since they're all built to withstand hurricanes.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.980
I dunno. Some of 'em look pretty beat already.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:50.150
It's an old town.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.970
Have you been here before, Miss Sela?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.110
Nope, it's all new to me.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:07.540
Miss Sela?

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.740
I'm gonna check things out over there.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.440
Miss Haruka will scold you if you skip the scouting!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.930
I'll make sure to look around!

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:15.850
Miss Sela!

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:16.880
Oh, just let her go.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.250
Maybe she's hungry.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.300
Don't lump her with yourself!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.820
What?! Stupid-head!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.160
Shut up, dingbat!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.560
What?!

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.140
What do ya mean, "what," you overgrown pet?!

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.430
"Sela's Road"?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.210
Hey! What are ya doing? Let's go!

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.730
Okay!

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.930
Look! It's Dunk Mask!

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.570
So it is! It's Dan JD!

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.110
There's Iceman Hotty!

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.790
Hey! What the heck?!

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:46.910
It's him!

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.250
What's wrong?

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.920
Oh, it's nothing.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.980
I knew it! Now that Dan JD's here, we can really get excited!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.300
He said it! It wouldn't be Basquash without you guys!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.640
D-Damn right it wouldn't!

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.420
Can you write your name here?

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.220
I'm collecting everyone's autograph!

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.260
Your wish is my command.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.520
C'mon, hurry up!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.190
I beg your pardon.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.490
Bel said that the blogosphere was turning upside down over this, and I guess he was right!

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.550
Huh? Mr. Iceman?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.870
What? Did the iceberg wander off by himself somewhere too?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.690
You guys are falling apart.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:31.500
Really!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.500
Here! Put your name and address here, please.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.840
As expected, there are some pretty nice machines around here.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.940
Hey, Ganz!

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.250
Yeah? What's next?

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.430
Take a look at this.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.390
This town's really interesting.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:56.680
It's got a Sela's Road, a Sela's Brook, in fact, there's "Sela's" all over the place!

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.510
Well, what do ya know.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.480
Sela?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.320
Mom...

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.690
So this is where you are.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:42.210
Well, I didn't expect you to show your face at the house after all this time.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.040
Master.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.090
Seems like you've been doing well lately.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.370
Make this one for the history books.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:57.120
I don't care if you knock the town down around you.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.620
You sure?

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.200
It's an old town.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.270
We've got insurance. I doubt anyone will complain.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:08.300
Besides, there's some pretty big bets riding on your team.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.930
How many times must you crush something precious to me before you're satisfied?

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.770
You resemble her now.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.890
You have no right to talk about Mom!

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:29.280
Do you have any idea what Mom went through after the family drove her out?!

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.330
How much pain she died in?!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.510
All because I'm a female so I can't inherit! No other reason!

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.780
Stop right there!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.090
Our conversation isn't over-

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.140
I'm looking forward to seeing you.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.320
Mr. Falcon!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.350
Those of you who are with the press, please leave.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.230
You will be a distraction to our guests.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.550
Don't say that!

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.590
Just one photo!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.590
C'mon! Give us an interview with Falcon!

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.320
Please!

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.660
What a ruckus.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.080
Nothing less for the one-and-only Falcon, though.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.410
Mind if I borrow that?

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.270
What?

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.780
Yes?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.530
Your wine has arrived, Mr. Falcon.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.140
Ah, I see.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.840
A message was delivered with it.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.060
Iceman!

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:44.760
I wonder where Miss Sela and Mr. Iceman went?

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.960
Who... knows?!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.210
That's dangerous, Mr. Dan!

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.490
Don't call me Mr. Dan!

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.470
Listen, we're not here to play around!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.020
There's a flutter in the wind...

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.720
So fast! And precise...

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.220
This is the sound of dribbling!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.320
Hey!

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:38.160
Hey, I hear Team Bigbear arrived!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.350
Starfire too!

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.930
Let's go see!

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:52.080
People came here on the wind from all over the place,

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.850
ready to play on a whole new level from anyone we've faced so far...

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.750
I've got to keep that in mind.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.000
Man, I'm sleepy.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.620
Man, I'm starving.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:04.230
Ow!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.340
I'm surprised you managed to get in here.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.710
Oh, that wasn't difficult.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.750
I said I'd trade him one of your secrets.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.880
I know something you don't!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.370
You bastard! What did you tell him?

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.550
Does it matter?

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:38.110
Once the match begins, we won't have the opportunity to talk like this.

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:44.980
Do you want me to congratulate you for making it to the championships?

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.570
Or are you here to rant about your grudge?

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:53.090
It's true that I hated you.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.610
There's no counting how many times I've killed you in my dreams.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.900
Maybe it's better to get shoes specially made for these conditions after all...

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:14.630
We can just leave that stuff to the boobs.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:17.320
Mr. Dan, look properly!

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.100
You're looking too hard!

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.730
Those players are big! They look strong!

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:28.320
Being big doesn't make you good.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.790
I wanna eat something big!

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.060
The wind's direction, and its strength...

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:43.670
I think that will have a huge effect on how we play.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.510
Silly Mr. Dan...

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.700
I've got to be the responsible one here...

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:07.150
What's that over there?

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:38.860
I can hear it.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.290
The murmur and roar of many people.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.760
The town's tension and expectations before the festival...

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.730
I'm sure this is where the opening ceremonies are going to be held.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:50.730
And it's Dan, with a fifth lap of one minute and forty-five seconds!

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.980
Sweet! A new world record!

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.960
Mr. Dan! Do you know what you're doing?!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.070
Incredible players have gathered here from all over the world!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.610
They're a level up from the teams you've played so far!

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.890
We've got to investigate as much as we can!

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:06.970
Are you okay, Mr. Dan-

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.440
That hurt! Dammit!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.000
No kidding!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.130
You again, Dunk Mask!

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.000
You again, Idol Red!

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.840
It's Rouge.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.590
You gonna sing at the opening ceremonies?

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.320
Man, sounds just like something a pop idol would do.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.940
I <i>am</i> an idol.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.960
And I'm in the middle of rehearsals right now!

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.590
What do ya mean, "three hearses tall"?

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.740
Make sense, will ya?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:32.970
Rehearsals!

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.390
You can watch if you want.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:35.900
I'll let you in as a special favor.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:36.690
No thanks.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.120
Do you know how much one of my fans would pay for that chance?!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.290
I'm not one of your fans!

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.740
I am!

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:48.250
I... erm, I'm an Eclipse fan!

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:51.750
But the gauntlet has already been thrown down.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:55.530
So, Mr. Dan, you and Miss Rouge should stop getting along so well with each other.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.870
When did I ever get along with Red?!

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.230
What's gotten into him?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.170
Who knows? He's been acting weird all day.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.140
The gauntlet has been thrown down.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.450
Oh, that's right! Did you hear about the prize?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.920
I couldn't care less.

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:14.420
Really? I reckon it's something that would psych you up.

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:15.560
Rouge?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.690
Where are you, Rouge?

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:17.570
Thought so!

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.640
I better go, or I'll never hear the end of it!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.610
Well, I'll see you at the match, Dunk Mask.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.800
Yeah, later, Idol Red!

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:26.200
Rouge!

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.370
Where were you?

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.550
The break ended several-

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.860
I got lost.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:52.940
Dan JD, is it?

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.900
You've still got an attachment to a player who was dropped?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.610
Why don't I let you see it too?

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:01.650
What a legend is.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:05.750
Even though you speak so highly of him,

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.640
I've yet to see him as anything other than a wild monkey.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.710
I see.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:13.960
Then perhaps I should've made the first prize a mountain of bananas.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:21.930
But the prize this time is something that he'll like nearly as much as bananas, I'm sure.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.470
Good!

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.180
Every last one of 'em is perfect!

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.750
Miyuki!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:28.910
Come here!

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.520
There's been an announcement!

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:31.520
What?

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:32.960
What?

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.930
Hey! Let's finish up and head back already!

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.320
Yeah! I'm gonna eat you if I get any hungrier, stupid-head!

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.980
Feel free.

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:46.020
Hey, what's got you so riled up, anyway?

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:47.960
I'm not angry.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.310
Yes you are!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.980
I'm not angry. I'm fed up.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:54.120
Huh? Fed up?

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.920
Yes, I'm fed up.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:58.440
With our whole team, not just you, Mr. Dan.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.330
Mr. Iceman and Miss Sela too...

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:02.340
You're all scattered everywhere!

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:03.290
It doesn't matter.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.760
I'll scout out the whole town even if I have to do it by myself!

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.940
But you know, the wind hasn't started blowing yet.

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:13.470
The wind?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.690
You said it yourself.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:18.770
Many winds are gathered into one!

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.570
You're not heading back?

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:34.710
You know, Crawly, I don't remember how Mom looked when she smiled.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.050
I can only remember her crying.

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:46.430
Mommy! Mommy!

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.430
Sela.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:53.720
Tell me! Why did Mommy have to die?!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.260
Answer me!

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:08.390
So? Are you serious about killing me this time?

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:12.490
It's true that because you repudiated me, I never became a legend.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:15.880
And so I hated you enough to want to kill you.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.210
I repeat:

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:28.440
A moment ago, the OCB Commission revealed that the first prize in the Championships

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.880
will be a pass to play in the Lunar League.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:33.850
James...

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.580
What are you plotting this time?

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.120
Amazing! The Lunar League!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:39.980
Hear that, Mr. Dan-

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:48.990
Mr. Dan?

00:17:56.400 --> 00:18:00.210
At that moment, I felt the wind blowing.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.890
As Mr. Dan dribbled, he was almost like...

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.430
Almost like... a whirlwind given form!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:39.920
Basquash!

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.590
Princess!

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:44.580
Jiiya, stay under!

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:02.060
Dan?

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.690
{ah sound}And I just finished servicing him too!

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.070
Learn some restraint, Dan!

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:00.530
That hurts!

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:01.580
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:04.740
Silly Mr. Dan.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:05.970
You can say that again.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:09.790
When it comes to Dan, the best-laid plots never seem to matter much.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.070
Plots?

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:14.090
Oh, never mind.

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:15.390
Shall we go?

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:18.010
So says the child who refused to move all this time.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:22.560
I'll do it for myself. That's all.

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:28.370
So, are you gonna kill me, Iceman?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.670
No, I won't kill you.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:34.150
I'll win against you and I'll leave you alive; then, I'll leave you behind me.

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.900
You've changed!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.480
Someone taught me to not run away, that's all.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.800
Dan!

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.650
Dan!

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.180
All right!

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:03.260
Let's go for it!

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:09.190
The scattered winds gathered into one to produce an incredible power!

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:15.200
Okay! Let's aim for the League! The League!

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.820
Dan sure has gotten pumped up.

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.480
It's the moon! It's a moon passport, yo!

